{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Cech&limit=10&title=The Catalyst","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":[{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"catalyst ","subTitle":"RNA and the quest to unlock life's deepest secrets "},{"@type":"alternative","title":"RNA and the quest to unlock life's deepest secrets"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Ribonucleic acid and the quest to unlock life's deepest secrets"}],"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Cech, Thomas,","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}],"nameIdentifier":"https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJvhvDhBpQ7q3W9hrch4MP"},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"still image"}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2024"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2024"},"issuance":"monographic","edition":"First edition."},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York, NY :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"W. W. Norton & Company,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":[2024],"issuance":"single unit"}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":[{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@authority":"marccategory","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"marcsmd","#text":"regular print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"292 pages : illustrations ; 24 cm"},{"form":{"@type":"Illustrative content","#text":"illustration"}}],"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Exploring the most transformative breakthroughs in biology since the discovery of the double helix, a Nobel Prize-winning scientist unveils the RNA age. For over half a century, DNA has dominated science and the popular imagination as the \"secret of life.\" But over the last several decades, a quiet revolution has taken place. In a series of breathtaking discoveries, the biochemist Thomas R. Cech and a diverse cast of scientists have revealed that RNA -- long overlooked as the passive servant of DNA -- sits at the center of biology's greatest mysteries: How did life begin? What makes us human? Why do we get sick and grow old? In this volume, Cech brings together years of research to demonstrate that RNA is the true key to understanding life on Earth, from its very origins to our future in the twenty-first century. -- Provided by publisher."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Introduction: The age of RNA -- Part I: The search -- The messenger -- Splice of life -- Going it alone -- The shape of a shapeshifter -- The mothership -- Origins -- Part II: The cure -- Is the fountain of youth a death trap? -- As the worm turns -- Precise parasites, sloppy copies -- RNA versus RNA -- Running with scissors -- Epilogue: The future of RNA."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Thomas R. Cech."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (pages [251]-280) and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"RNA"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Genomics"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"RNA"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Genomics"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"ARN"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Génomique"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SCIENCE / Life Sciences / Biochemistry"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SCIENCE / Biotechnology"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SCIENCE / History"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SCIENCE / Life Sciences / Molecular Biology"},